  "Question": "Without changing the value of the algebraic fraction, multiply both the numerator and denominator of \\((0.2x+0.5)/(0.3x-0.1)\\) by 10 to obtain \\((ax+5)/(bx-1)\\). What is \\(a+b\\)?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "5",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Multiplying the numerator \\(0.2x+0.5\\) by 10 gives \\(2x+5\\), and multiplying the denominator \\(0.3x-0.1\\) by 10 gives \\(3x-1\\). Thus, \\(a=2\\), \\(b=3\\), and \\(a+b=5\\).",
